package tech.appard.hvala.shared.core.i18n.content

internal const val privacyPolicyContentEn: String = """
Requirements for the placement and content of ads

1. The ad must be legitimate
Do not place offers, conditions or information in ads that violate the legislation of Montenegro or the rights of third parties, or contribute to such violations (for example, the requirement to transfer a passport as collateral).
You have the right to place ads only about those goods, services, vacancies, objects and other offers (hereinafter referred to as "goods") in respect of which you have all the necessary rights, licenses, registrations, permits, certificates, etc.
Before placing an ad, you must ensure the legality of all its elements (including photos, videos, links to third-party sites, when they are allowed, etc.). You will be responsible for any violations of the law or the rights of third parties that you have committed, yourself.

2. The information in the ad must be reliable and complete
We consider it a gross violation of the HVALA rules to place any information in the ad that may mislead about your product or the terms of your offer.
This also means that the ad must contain an up-to-date phone number where you can be contacted.
If your offer is required by law to contain any information, you must specify them.
You are solely responsible for the distribution of an ad that lacks mandatory information or contains false information.

3. The ad must match the categories on HVALA
Place ads only for those products for which there is a thematic category on HVALA. Do not place ads about accepting gifts, ordering services, collecting financial assistance, dating, finding, losing, buying or searching. Exceptions: you can place an ad for the purchase of real estate only in the "Real Estate" category, an ad for a job search or an employee – only in the "Work" category.
Ads can be placed within the same category using only one profile (including if you operate within the same company or joint business, family or in the interests of your friends).
It is prohibited to place several products in one ad, except in cases where they make up a set or correspond to the same category. If several products corresponding to the same category are placed in the ad, a price must be indicated for each product.
Exceptions: – in the categories "Real Estate", "Transport", "Vacancies" and "Phones" you are required to place a separate ad for each offer.
We have the right to set limits on the number of ads placed for free for certain categories and regions (limit) so that users, especially from large regions, can see offers from different sellers. If the limit is reached within 30 and/or 365 calendar days prior to the placement of the ad, the subsequent submission of a new or activation of a previously created ad in the relevant categories and regions is possible for a fee, in accordance with the Terms of paid ad placement.

4. The offer must be specific, existing and relevant
Place ads about a specific existing consumer-value product. For example, you can't sell a doughnut hole on HVALA or rent an apartment on Mars.
If you place an ad for the sale of a product, the product must be available to you, if you place an ad for a service, you must be ready to provide it, if you place an ad for the rental of real estate, you must be ready to transfer it to the tenant, etc. We allow the placement of goods on pre-order, including from abroad, and goods that will soon go on sale. Placement of products made to order is possible in the subcategories "Furniture and interior", "Repair and construction", "Tableware and kitchen goods", "Spare parts". If you offer a custom-made product, when placing it in the "Availability" parameter, select the "Custom-made" value, if such an option is available in the HVALA interface.
In some categories, it may be possible to specify the number of items in stock. If this feature is available in the HVALA interface, you can indicate that there are several units of the product available and mark the exact quantity of the available product. If you have not specified the quantity, it is considered that there is only one product in stock.
Keep up-to-date information about the quantity of goods in stock in the HVALA profile. The ad may be removed from publication, unless otherwise provided by the rules or in the HVALA interface. The removal of an ad from publication due to the end of the product in stock is equivalent to its removal from publication by the user himself. If the product is still in stock, update the information about its quantity in the HVALA profile.
If you have sold a product or your offer has ceased to be relevant for other reasons, remove the ad from publication as soon as possible. Do not change the content of a previously published ad. In particular, do not upload photos of other goods or real estate. For a new offer, create a new ad.
If there is a technical possibility and only if the automatic activation function is enabled in the profile, HVALA automatically activates ads after the next maximum period of their placement has expired. If you do not need automatic activation of ads, disable it in your profile or contact support specialists.
Do not place ads without the purpose of concluding a deal in relation to exactly the product that is specified in the ad (fictitious ads). It is forbidden to place ads for the purposes of lead generation — obtaining contact details of potential buyers. Enhanced checks of the relevance of ads are constantly carried out to identify fictitious ones.
Remember that placing an ad may entail for you an obligation to a potential buyer to conclude and execute a transaction in accordance with civil law.
Do not place general advertising information in ads without a specific offer. The placement of ads on HVALA is carried out in order to inform users about the possibility and conditions of transactions. The ads themselves, as well as the information contained in them, are not aimed at forming and maintaining interest in a particular person, his product or service.

5. It is forbidden to place repeated ads
You can place only one valid ad for one product. We are considering placing repeated ads (duplicates) as a gross violation of HVALA rules.
This means that you cannot place repeated ads (duplicates) about the offer of the same product in different cities or districts. 
The placement of a repeat ad (duplicate) will also be considered if:
you remove the ad from publication or delete it (including before the expiration of its placement), and then place a new ad with the same product, including in another region or in another category;
you will edit the published ad, replacing the offered product with another one, and then place a new ad that will offer the product from the original version of the old ad.
If the ad parameters match the same parameters of another previously placed ad, a later ad is considered repeated and can be blocked.


      Data Processing Policy

1. General provisions
HVALA ("we") processes the personal data of registered and unregistered users – everyone who accesses our website and mobile applications, as well as contacts HVALA by phone numbers listed on the website ("users", or "you").
By providing us with personal data, you consent to their processing in accordance with this policy.

2. Definitions
Personal data – any information relating directly or indirectly to a specific or identifiable individual (subject of personal data).
Personal data processing is the implementation of actions or a set of actions in relation to personal data, including collection, recording, systematization, accumulation, storage, clarification, updating and modification, extraction, use, provision, access, blocking, deletion and destruction – both with and without the use of automated data processing tools.
We may process your data in the listed ways for the purposes set out in section 4 of this Policy.
The operator of personal data is a state body, municipal body, legal entity or individual, independently or jointly with other persons organizing and (or) processing personal data, as well as determining the purposes of processing personal data, the composition of personal data to be processed, actions (operations) performed with personal data.
We are the operator in relation to the personal data that we may receive in connection with your use of HVALA (including the website and mobile applications).

3. What data do we process
You provide us with personal data when:
• you register on HVALA;
• you use HVALA;
• pay for HVALA services;
• subscribe to newsletters;
• participate in events, research and surveys;
• write or call us (for example, when you contact support);
• communicate with other users;
• exercise rights or perform duties based on our terms and conditions.
We may receive your personal data from our partners in connection with the execution of a contract under which you are a party or beneficiary.
Your device automatically transmits technical data: information stored in cookies, information about the browser and its settings, date and time of access to HVALA, addresses of the requested pages, actions on the website or in the application, technical characteristics of the device, IP address, etc.
We process only general categories of personal data. We do not process biometric personal data and special categories of personal data. 

4. Purposes of personal data processing
• Providing you with the opportunity to use HVALA: create a profile, place ads, etc., and also, with your consent, provide you with the opportunity to use the services of our partners;
• Ensuring stable operation and safety of HVALA, improving user experience, quality of services and marketing activities;
• Prevention and suppression of violations of the law, HVALA Terms of Use and our other rules and conditions, including protection of users from fraudulent and other unfair actions;
• Fulfilling the obligations stipulated by the legislation (for example, for accounting, tax reporting, responding to requests from government agencies);
• Providing answers to your requests;
• Sending marketing messages about HVALA and our partners;
• Organizing your participation in events, research and surveys of HVALA and our partners.
If you contact us as a representative of a government agency or the media, we process the data specified in the request (surname, first name, patronymic, email address, phone number, position, place of work) in order to fulfill the obligations provided for by law and respond to your request.
If you contact us as a copyright holder, we process the data specified in the request (surname, first name, patronymic, email address, phone number, passport data, information confirming the existence of an exclusive right and your authority) in order to fulfill the obligations provided for by law and respond to your request.

5. Legal grounds for processing
We process your personal data:
• with your consent.
You consent to the processing of your personal data during registration and each time you log in to HVALA, as well as during the use of HVALA. For example, when you follow instructions in HVALA interfaces, click on special buttons, write messages or perform other actions. You consent for 1 year from the date of deletion of your HVALA profile or, if you are an unregistered user, from the date of achievement of the purpose of processing personal data.
• for the conclusion, execution, modification or termination of the contract – the Terms of Use of HVALA and our other terms and conditions, and rules, as well as your contracts with our partners;
• to exercise the rights and legitimate interests of HVALA or third parties, if your rights and freedoms are not violated;
• to perform the duties assigned to us by law.

6. Transfer to third parties
We may transfer personal data or entrust their processing to third parties if it is necessary to provide you with HVALA services or, in the case of providing other services, with your separate consent.
We may transfer your personal data to our partners who participate in providing certain services to you, as well as to government agencies if we are required to provide them with your personal data in accordance with the law.

7. Data placement on HVALA
When you publish ads, reviews or information in your profile on HVALA, personal data as part of such information becomes available to an indefinite circle of people. You disclose such data yourself without giving us, as the operator of personal data, a separate consent. HVALA does not distribute your personal data.
The purpose for which users post data on HVALA is to establish contact with a potential buyer (client, employer) who is interested in concluding a deal on the ad. Users do not have the right to process the data of other users for any other purposes. This means that:
• you cannot call or send messages to users to offer your products or services;
• you cannot copy user data to post it on other services;
• you cannot use HVALA users' information for scoring purposes.

8. Storage of personal data
We record, systematize, accumulate, store, clarify (update, change), extract your personal data using databases.
We store your data in accordance with the terms of data processing necessary to achieve the processing purposes specified in section 4 of this Policy.

9. Updates to this Data Processing Policy
We may update this Data Processing Policy from time to time.
We will notify you of any material changes to this Policy by posting a notification in our application (on our website) or by sending an email to your email address.

    
"""
